 explodes things the great  fairy mask attracts stray fairies  another teaches you how to dance one to  lead small animals another to run faster  and look like a bunny some turn you into  other races like the D goo mask and  Goron mask these help to solve puzzles  and more easily navigate some areas  depending on the skills ascribed to the  mask speaking of making life easier if  you play Majora's Mask 3d on the new  Nintendo 3ds you'll benefit from the  system's extra features the added C  stick lets you change the camera angle  at will so tracking quick moving bosses  in combat and writing Epona are much  easier this makes playing on older 3ds  models feel a little clunky so if you  have to choose the new 3ds is the way to  go for a better experience other small  changes include more save points and a  better song of double-time that lets you  fast forward to it ever hour you choose  within a same-day window but by far the  best changes to the Bombers notebooks  which are more detailed and  comprehensive these books are your  quests log where you keep track of  uncompleted and failed tasks successful  ones and the rumors you've heard about  new ones you can also keep track of the  specific day and time events happen and  let you set alarms for them this is an  amazing addition that makes housekeeping  way more manageable and lets you keep  track of what items you get and when  without having to take written notes  yourself with better ways to manage your  time majora's mask 3d is friendlier in  shorter play times you don't need to sit  down for hours and scribble out your own  notes every time you play and it's a  welcome addition to the handheld's  library it's still the odd mind-bending  classic but with new additions that make  it much more enjoyable and fresh feeling  after so many years
 

